            "review_title": "Review at Sushi Hokkaido Sachi (Phan Xich Long)",
            "review_text": "CatherineWelly\nWellington, New Zealand71 contributions\n0\nDon’t be in any kind of rush\nAug 2019 • Solo\nFish was fresh and there were many things to choose from the menu. I didn’t enjoy the wasabi here thou, felt like they added grated radish and ginger into it.\nWhat I dislike was their speed. Waited for 5 minutes for a table while there were many empty seats as it was almost 9pm. Food came one by one even though I did asked for ‘all together’ while ordering. When I asked again for my other dishes, the response I got was “Please wait, there’re coming”. Well yes I know it’s coming but that was not the point. I came by myself and asked for all food to come at once because I had no one to talk with or I was in a rush or I didn’t want to wait for food or any other reasons on the planet. Why couldn’t someone in hospo understand this basic thing? \n4 stars for food, 2 for service!\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 21, 2019",
